 "description": {
  "lang": "en",
  "script": "Latn",
  "text": "Beneath the Lion's Gaze: A Novel by Maaza Mengiste \"An important novel, rich in compassion for its anguished characters.\" —The New York Times Book Review This memorable, heartbreaking story opens in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia, 1974, on the eve of a revolution. Yonas kneels in his mother’s prayer room, pleading to his god for an end to the violence that has wracked his family and country. His father, Hailu, a prominent doctor, has been ordered to report to jail after helping a victim of state-sanctioned torture to die. And Dawit, Hailu’s youngest son, has joined an underground resistance movement—a choice that will lead to more upheaval and bloodshed across a ravaged Ethiopia."
 },
